Tic-Tac-Toe Game

A simple and interactive Tic-Tac-Toe game built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

The game allows two players to take turns placing X and O on a 3×3 grid. The game automatically checks for winning combinations and declares the winner when a player gets three matching symbols in a row, column, or diagonal. If all boxes are filled without a winner, the game ends in a draw.

Features
🎮 Two-player gameplay
❌ Different styling for X and O
🏆 Automatic winner detection
🤝 Draw detection
🔄 Reset Game and New Game buttons
🚫 Prevents players from selecting an already-used box
✨ Hover effects for available boxes
📱 Simple and responsive layout
Technologies Used
HTML — Game structure
CSS — Styling and layout
JavaScript — Game logic, player turns, win/draw detection, and game controls

This project was created as a beginner-friendly JavaScript project to practice DOM manipulation, event listeners, conditional logic, arrays, and functions.
